ited sovereignty and no right of return for Palestinian refugees. The plan has been met with criticism from the international community, with Pope Francis calling on the US to respect the status quo in Jerusalem.\n\n**Violent Protests Expected**\n\nThe recognition of Jerusalem as Israel's capital is expected to spark violent protests in the region. Manuel Hassassian, the Palestinian representative to the UK, has called the decision the \"kiss of death\" to the peace process. The move is seen as a further escalation of tensions in the region and has raised concerns about the future of the peace process.\n\nOverall, these recent news stories highlight",
